import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Retro — tensor-valued derives (ADR 0012): the $leaf: channel lands","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — tensor-valued derives (ADR 0012): the `$leaf:` channel lands","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/tensor-derives.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/tensor-derives.md"}'),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/tensor-derives.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-tensor-valued-derives-adr-0012-the-leaf-channel-lands" tabindex="-1">Retro — tensor-valued derives (ADR 0012): the <code>$leaf:</code> channel lands <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-tensor-valued-derives-adr-0012-the-leaf-channel-lands" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — tensor-valued derives (ADR 0012): the $leaf: channel lands”">​</a></h1><p><strong>ADR</strong>: <code>project/adrs/0012-tensor-derives.md</code>. <strong>Depends on</strong>: <code>project/retros/weightspace-fold.md</code> (the measured gate-by-gate refusal — gate 4, the last <em>capability</em> blocker), <code>project/retros/derive-root-ops.md</code> (the residual after <code>sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code>), ADR 0004 (the <code>dspec</code> DSL extended).</p><h2 id="what-the-refusal-measured-and-what-changed" tabindex="-1">What the refusal measured, and what changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-refusal-measured-and-what-changed" aria-label="Permalink to “What the refusal measured, and what changed”">​</a></h2><p>The weight-space lane measured the conv+BN fold as <em>structurally derivable but domain-blocked</em>: the synthesizer fit <code>W&#39; = W·scale</code> and <code>b&#39; = (b−μ)·scale + β</code> given a <code>scale</code> leaf, the DSL learned to spell <code>scale = γ·rsqrt(σ²+ε)</code> over scalars — and the value domain <code>int | float</code> refused the per-channel <em>tensor</em> <code>scale</code> with a measured <code>TypeError: unhashable type: &#39;numpy.ndarray&#39;</code> in the synthesizer&#39;s fingerprinting (gate 4). This round lands the seam ADR 0012 chooses, nothing more:</p><ul><li><strong><code>mlopt_core.laws.cond</code></strong> — a pushed <strong>tensor algebra</strong>, <code>register_tensor_algebra(source=, mint=, ops=, key=)</code>: core imports no array library, so a tensor value is an <em>opaque payload</em> the adapter&#39;s registrations create, transform and name — the same sink direction as <code>mlopt_core.ops</code>&#39; binding tables and <code>register_value_shape</code>. Two new expr ops: <code>(&quot;tval&quot;, T)</code> (a bound leaf&#39;s tensor value through <code>source</code>) and <code>(&quot;tapp&quot;, name, e…)</code> (the generic apply into the pushed <code>ops</code> table — <code>reshape</code>, <code>exp</code>, … — so the vocabulary boundary is the table, not the grammar). The <code>_DUNOPS</code>/<code>_DBINOPS</code> handlers gain a tensor tier: scalars keep today&#39;s semantics; a non-scalar operand dispatches to <code>ops[op]</code> when registered, else to the Python operator (which array backends already overload — only <code>math.*</code>-backed <code>sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code> <em>need</em> the table). And the <strong><code>$leaf:NAME</code> spec key</strong>: the expr&#39;s value is packaged as a <em>term</em> — <code>Const(v)</code> for a scalar, <code>Param(name, shape)</code> through <code>mint</code> for a tensor — emitted under the bare metavar key, so the RHS pattern&#39;s term metavar resolves it at instantiate time. <code>mint</code>&#39;s name must be deterministic in content (certificate replay re-runs the derive).</li><li><strong><code>egraph/core.py</code> <code>apply_rule</code></strong> — non-<code>$attr:</code> keys in a derive&#39;s output are <em>term</em> bindings: interned via <code>add_term</code> so <code>subst</code> stays uniform (metavar → eid) for the recorded <code>ProofEdge</code>. Term-level sites (<code>instantiate_pattern</code>, <code>_term_instantiate</code>, <code>apply_rewrite_at</code>) needed no change — <code>subst[name]</code> already drops a bound term in place.</li><li><strong><code>mlopt_core.cost.basic</code></strong> — <code>batch_norm</code> joins <code>_OP_FLOPS</code> at 4 (sub + mul + mul + add ≈ four elementwise passes over <code>n_out</code>; the measured gate-6 gap). <code>group_norm</code>/<code>instance_norm</code> stay unpriced — unmeasured here.</li><li><strong><code>mlopt_discovery.dspec_synth</code></strong> — fingerprints box every value through <code>_vkey</code> (scalars by value, sequences elementwise, payloads through the algebra&#39;s <code>key</code> — or by identity when none is registered, so a tensor fit without <code>key</code> refuses honestly rather than crashing); <code>(&quot;tval&quot;, T)</code> joins the leaf bank when a <code>source</code> is registered; <code>tval</code> counts as reading bound for the no-constant guard; <code>_vbin</code>/<code>_vun</code> mirror the tensor dispatch so value-level signatures agree with <code>eval_derive</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="the-measured-delta-probe-gate-4-re-run" tabindex="-1">The measured delta (probe gate 4 re-run) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-measured-delta-probe-gate-4-re-run" aria-label="Permalink to “The measured delta (probe gate 4 re-run)”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>signal</th><th>before</th><th>after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>tensor_sample_error</code></td><td><code>TypeError: unhashable type: &#39;numpy.ndarray&#39;</code></td><td><strong>None</strong></td></tr><tr><td>scale as a <code>$leaf:</code> derive</td><td>unspellable</td><td><strong><code>scale_mints_as_leaf: True</code></strong> — <code>scale__aecaec8b1d30</code> mints a <code>Param</code> through <code>mint</code>, value-exact against <code>γ/√(σ²+ε)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>tensor_synth_fit</code></td><td>crash</td><td><strong><code>{&#39;Wn&#39;: (&#39;mul&#39;, (&#39;attr&#39;,&#39;g&#39;), (&#39;tval&#39;,&#39;w&#39;))}</code></strong> — the synthesizer mints a tensor derive</td></tr><tr><td><code>batch_norm</code> price</td><td>absent (default)</td><td><strong><code>4·n_out</code></strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>batch_norm</code> in a law LHS</td><td>absent</td><td><strong>unchanged</strong> — content, not capability (the law is derivable next; the no-hardcoding rule holds)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>End-to-end verified at both instantiate sites: an e-graph <code>apply_rule</code> fires a <code>$leaf:</code> rule and lands the minted <code>Param</code>&#39;s enode in the class, and term-level <code>apply_rewrite_at</code> replays the derive <strong>deterministically</strong> (same minted name twice — the replay contract).</p><h2 id="what-this-does-and-does-not-buy" tabindex="-1">What this does and does not buy <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-does-and-does-not-buy" aria-label="Permalink to “What this does and does not buy”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Closed</strong>: weight-space refusal reason 2 (the <code>int|float</code> value domain) and reason 4 (<code>batch_norm</code> unpriced). The fold&#39;s remaining blockers are <em>content</em>: a <code>batch_norm</code> LHS law — derivable now — and synth enumeration depth ≥4 over the 7-attr bank (a budget question, <code>derive-root-ops.md</code> item b).</li><li><strong>Known limits</strong> (ADR 0012 states them): <code>meta.synthesize_rules</code> still requires RHS <em>term</em> metavars LHS-bound, so a <code>$leaf:</code> rule cannot be auto-composed (the <code>@i:</code> placeholder machinery is attr-only); <code>mint</code>&#39;s determinism is a documented contract, not an enforced one; a <code>$leaf:</code> value that is neither scalar nor mintable declines — no third landing zone.</li><li><code>DEFAULT</code> untouched: no law changed; the only extraction-visible delta is the <code>batch_norm</code> price.</li></ul><h2 id="gates" tabindex="-1">Gates <a class="header-anchor" href="#gates" aria-label="Permalink to “Gates”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>pytest tests/test_derive_laws.py tests/test_cond_laws.py tests/test_discovery_dspec_synth.py</code> — <strong>167 passed</strong> (incl. new <code>TestTensorDerives</code> ×10 in derive_laws — tval/tapp dispatch, the <code>$leaf:</code> mint, declines, JSON round-trip, e-graph firing, deterministic term replay — and ×4 in dspec_synth — the tensor fit, the no-<code>key</code> honest refusal, leaf seeding, <code>_vkey</code> boxing).</li><li><code>pytest tests/test_law_serialize.py tests/test_lemma_certificates.py tests/test_egraph_internals.py tests/test_rules.py</code> — <strong>141 passed</strong> (the <code>apply_rule</code> subst path, cert replay and rule serialization are undisturbed).</li><li><code>ruff check</code> / <code>ruff format --check</code> on the touched shipped files — clean. <code>ty check</code> — <strong>0 errors</strong>. <code>lint-imports</code> — <strong>4/4 kept</strong> (core stays torch-free <em>and</em> numpy-free: the algebra is pushed, never imported).</li></ul>`,12)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};